If a patient has an objective-opioid-withdrawal-sign then every clinician should conduct a standard-buprenorphine-initiation for the patient.
If a patient has an uncontrolled-opioid-withdrawal-symptom during a standard-buprenorphine-initiation then every clinician should increase a buprenorphine-dose for the patient under a clinical-supervision after a standard-buprenorphine-titration-interval.
Every standard-buprenorphine-titration-interval should approximate 2 hours.
